This image demonstrates the inflammatory response and cellular uptake of Nano-11 at the injection site 24 hours after intramuscular administration. When Nano-11 is co-injected with ovalbumin (OVA), there is a notable recruitment of Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages and MHCII+ antigen-presenting cells, which actively internalize the AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red). In contrast, soluble OVA alone induces minimal inflammatory cell infiltration. This supports Nano-11's role in attracting immune cells and facilitating antigen delivery, initiating the adaptive immune response.